# Author / packaging identity

When writing or updating `debian/changelog`, `debian/control`, `debian/copyright`,
or matching packaging fields (RPM Packager/URL, …), resolve identity as follows.

## Changelog trailer (`-- Name (comment) <email>`)

1. Take the current login name (`id -un` / `$USER`, e.g. `lenik`).
2. From `gpg -k` / `gpg --list-secret-keys`, pick a key that:
   - has a **secret** key available, and
   - whose **uid name** matches the login (**case-insensitive**; compare the
     name part before `(` / `<`, e.g. login `lenik` ↔ uid `Lenik (…)`).
3. If several match, prefer:
   - **no passphrase** on the secret key (gpg-agent `KEYINFO` protection `-`,
     not `P`), then
   - the **most recently created/updated** key.
4. From that uid:
   - **name** → uid name field
   - **(comment)** → uid comment field (omit `()` if empty)
   - **email** → uid email field

Example: uid `Lenik (谢继雷) <lenik@bodz.net>` →
`Lenik (谢继雷) <lenik@bodz.net>`.

## Maintainer (`debian/control`)

Same display name (and comment) as the changelog trailer.

**Exception — login `lenik`:** keep the name/comment, but set email to
`<PACKAGE@bodz.net>` where `PACKAGE` is the Debian source/package name
(lowercase), e.g. `Lenik (谢继雷) <zephyr@bodz.net>`. This splits traffic across
many packages.

## Homepage

All lowercase:

```text
https://github.com/<user>/<package>
```

`<user>` is the login (or GitHub handle in lowercase); `<package>` is the
package/project name in lowercase.

## Copyright / license

**AGPL-3** (AGPL-3.0-or-later / Debian `AGPL-3+`) **with the anti-AI supplemental
restriction** as in the project `LICENSE` (and the note in `debian/copyright`).
Do not drop the anti-AI block when scaffolding or ize-ing packaging files.
